 "notes": "E592 is the Excavations-sheet row of this same site (bracketed copy of the unit's components) but its point lies 447 m at 10.3 deg (valid); per the rule for other rows its tombs and caves take grid E592. Hard rule to apply: this places the unit's own features north of it. Own-row tombs: type not stated, no position. SWP III p. 4 El 'Aziriyeh (Bethany, linked in Stage 1b) is the village, not this unit, but within 2 km (S3458 el-'Eizariya/Bethany, 1834 m): tomb of Lazarus given S3458's point; rock-cut tombs 'east of Bethany' coded words E relative to other. The Bethlehem text on the same page is another place and ignored. Duplicate pairs S3334/E573, S3575/E698 recorded per row. Survey entry and first publication (Peleg 2009i) not accessed."
